# The shipper merges every pull request whose required verdicts pass at head,
# through the merge queue. The repo's own rule files (.decisions/, AGENTS.md,
# CLAUDE.md, .fabrika.jsonc, the design manifest) are not listed here; they
# stay gated by the required governance verdict (`governedRoots` in
# .fabrika.jsonc). Huey can hold any pull request with the `ready-for:human`
# label, which the `ci-required` check enforces in the queue.
#
# Fabrika's fixed control-plane boundary (fabrika-cli) names these paths, and
# its codeowners-cp guard requires them owned, so changes to workflows, agent
# settings and git hooks still need Huey's sign-off.
/.claude/                   @hueypov
/.github/                   @hueypov
**/lefthook*                @hueypov
**/.lefthook*               @hueypov

# Named by Fabrika's control-plane list; none exist here yet. The rows keep
# `fabrika guard codeowners-cp check` green and cover the paths if they appear.
/.claude-plugin/                @hueypov
/packages/ci-required/          @hueypov
/packages/fabrika-cli/src/ci/   @hueypov
/biome.jsonc                    @hueypov
/biome-plugins/                 @hueypov
